 You provide `render`, `data`, or both, depending on the area.
 
+## Native live voice adapters (candidate API v1)
+
+This candidate adds `ctx.registerLiveVoiceProvider(provider)`. It is not part of a
+released SDK contract yet: feature-detect the method and refuse an older host.
+The first consumer is a standalone Grok Voice adapter; OpenAI keeps its existing
+built-in path. The v1 broker descriptor targets a WebSocket/PCM transport, not a
+universal provider API or a replacement for OpenAI WebRTC.
+
+```js
+export default {
+  id: 'grok-native-provider',
+  defaultEnabled: false,
+  register(ctx) {
+    if (typeof ctx.registerLiveVoiceProvider !== 'function') {
+      throw new Error('This Desktop build does not support native voice adapters')
+    }
+    ctx.registerLiveVoiceProvider({
+      apiVersion: 1,
+      id: 'xai-oauth',
+      createSession: (bridge, handlers) => new GrokLiveSession(bridge, handlers)
+    })
+  }
+}
+```
+
+This registration adds **no composer action, titlebar button or settings page**.
+The existing voice-engine menu combines backend provider readiness with local
+adapter registration. Registration alone cannot authorize a provider, add a new
+backend broker, or enable an unadvertised provider. The current native consumer
+uses the existing `xai-oauth` configuration and narrow core broker.
+
+The host supplies an owner-bound bridge for canonical submission, exact receipt
+completion, busy state and ephemeral session minting. It never supplies durable
+OAuth credentials or generic access to core REST routes. The adapter owns only
+its provider transport and audio. It must implement `start`, `end`, `checkOwner`,
+`setMuted` and `stopTurn`; see the exported `NativeLive*` SDK types.
+
+The local host keeps `HermesGateway` / `CanonicalDesktopProtocol`: a fresh private
+one-use ticket is offered in WebSocket subprotocols, never left in the dial URL.
+Creation uses the canonical GUI launch policy (including model/provider, effort,
+speed, workspace provenance and owner route), not a legacy sidecar or a CLI-source
+fallback. Voice session creation reuses the normal create/publication door; stored
+chats reuse normal adoption/resume, including the Bot Chat name registry.
+
+Canonical admission receipts identify work with `admission_id` and `ref`, while
+`message.complete` carries `payload.admission_id`, `status` and `outcome`.
+A persisted row receipt is optional; the canonical gateway does not promise a
+`user_row_id` on admission. The current standalone API1 adapter only speaks a
+result when its accepted positive `user_row_id` matches a complete persisted turn.
+A `queued` receipt without that row is **accepted, chat-only**, even if a later
+completion acquires one. Do not manufacture a row or `client_turn_id`, infer
+identity from matching text, or automatically resubmit. Other uncorrelatable or
+unknown receipts direct the person to the chat without claiming cancellation.
+Canonical admission/event metadata passes through the bridge unchanged.
+
+Backend readiness, provider selection and the private mint capability must be
+implemented by the owning runtime/main process too. Registering this adapter on a
+canonical backend that does not advertise Grok is not enough; missing capability
+stays an explicit unavailable state. Do not widen generic REST authority or
+silently switch engines to work around it.
+
+Core owns one Grok call per window outside React. Composer views can unmount and
+reattach without redialling; actual conversation/owner changes, gateway loss,
+plugin unload and page teardown still revoke the call. Wake suspension and its
+indicator belong to that runtime, not to a mounted control. Hanging up or
+interrupting speech never cancels an accepted Hermes turn. This does not claim a
+new shared microphone-lease ABI for every legacy voice engine.
+
+A standalone adapter survives replacement of app files only while the installed
+app retains this contract. Until upstream integration, an official app update
+can remove the host seam. Do not describe the candidate as stock-Desktop or
+live-audio validated; run the offline adapter/owner/lifecycle tests and obtain a
+separate operator-started microphone/provider receipt before activation.
+
